---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';

const sections = ["When you send me a message", "Visit counts (no cookies)", "Google Analytics (only if you say yes)", "Tools on this site", "Your choices"];
const slug = (t: string) => t.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/^-|-$/g, '');
---

<Layout title="Privacy" description="What this site collects, why, and the choices you have.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8">
    <PageHero eyebrow="Privacy" aside="No ads, no data sold, and Google Analytics only if you say yes." rule>
      <Fragment slot="title">What this site collects, and why.</Fragment>
      A short, plain-language summary. I don't sell data, run ads, or build profiles of visitors.
    </PageHero>

    <section class="grid gap-12 pt-10 sm:pt-12 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,42rem)_14rem] lg:gap-16">
      <div class="prose-decode">
      <h2 id={slug("When you send me a message")}>When you send me a message</h2>
      <p>The Contact, Guest Lectures, Alert Me and RunSphere "Suggest a race" forms collect what you type: your name, email address, and message. They are delivered to my inbox through a form service called FormSubmit, which handles them on my behalf. I use them only to reply to you, and I don't share them with anyone else.</p>

      <h2 id={slug("Visit counts (no cookies)")}>Visit counts (no cookies)</h2>
      <p>I use Vercel Web Analytics to see anonymous totals: which pages are viewed, roughly which country visitors are in, and what device they use. It does not use cookies and does not follow you around the web.</p>

      <h2 id={slug("Google Analytics (only if you say yes)")}>Google Analytics (only if you say yes)</h2>
      <p>To understand which articles are useful and how people find them, I'd like to use Google Analytics. It stays switched off unless you click <strong>Accept</strong> on the notice at the bottom of the page. If you accept, Google sets cookies in your browser and records things like the pages you view, how long you stay, roughly where you are (city and country), the type of device and browser you use, and how you reached the site. It does not tell me who you are by name. Google processes this data under <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">its own terms</a>.</p>
      <p>If you click <strong>Decline</strong>, Google Analytics never loads.</p>

      <h2 id={slug("Tools on this site")}>Tools on this site</h2>
      <p>Interactive tools such as Governance Passport save your progress inside your own browser so you can come back later. That information stays on your device and is not sent to me or to anyone else.</p>

      <h2 id={slug("Your choices")}>Your choices</h2>
      <p>You can change your analytics choice at any time:</p>
      <p><button type="button" id="reset-consent" class="btn-primary px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold">Change my cookie choice</button></p>
      <p>To ask what I hold about you, or to have it deleted, email <a href="mailto:venu@decodewithvenu.com">venu@decodewithvenu.com</a>.</p>

      <p class="mt-12 text-sm text-mist-400">Last updated 7 October 2026.</p>
      </div>

      <aside class="hidden lg:block">
        <nav class="sticky top-10" aria-label="On this page">
          <p class="text-[13px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-cyan-glow">On this page</p>
          <ol class="mt-4 border-l border-edge/15 text-sm leading-snug">
            {sections.map((t) => (
              <li><a href={`#${slug(t)}`} class="-ml-px block border-l-2 border-transparent py-1.5 pl-4 text-mist-400 hover:border-cyan-glow hover:text-fg transition-colors">{t}</a></li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </nav>
      </aside>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
  document.getElementById('reset-consent')?.addEventListener('click', function () {
    if (window.resetCookieChoice) window.resetCookieChoice();
  });
</script>
